# No .gitattributes existed before this file -- line endings were left to
# core.autocrlf (Git for Windows' installer default, core.autocrlf=true),
# which normalizes to LF in the object store but converts to CRLF on
# checkout, AND masks CRLF-vs-LF differences from `git status`/`git diff`.
# That let three files under policies/ drift to CRLF in the working tree
# (introduced by some tool/editor after checkout, not by git itself) while
# git kept reporting "no changes" -- invisible to git, but fully visible to
# byte-reading tools like `opa fmt`/`opa check`, which is what surfaced it.
# Pinning eol=lf here makes checkout, not local editor/OS behavior, the
# single source of truth for these file types.
*.rego text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Never text-convert binary assets (self-hosted fonts under
# services/dashboard/src/assets/fonts -- see CLAUDE.md).
*.woff2 binary
